    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 records for the related BTK inhibitors rilzabrutinib and acalabrutinib show rapid oral absorption (Tmax ~0.5–1.0 h), consistent with non-limiting intestinal absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C35", "C38", "C40", "C42"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The L1/L2 low-F outcomes come from structurally unrelated molecules (peptidomimetics, nucleotides, antihistamines, etc.) and do not affirmatively establish F < 20% for the query scaffold; the fed-state low-F comparator melagatran is also structurally unrelated.",
