    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute F measurement is supplied.",
    "No direct absolute F value is supplied for acalabrutinib or rilzabrutinib; L4 provides permeability/solubility rather than systemic F.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance for the query are not directly quantified.",
    "Fed-state effects on the query are not directly measured; acalabrutinib L4 data are not fed-specific.",
    "Query solubility and formulation are not directly measured; acalabrutinib solubility values are for ASD formulations."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Flip to high: L4 provides affirmative intestinal absorption/permeability evidence for the closely related acalabrutinib scaffold, and L3 shows rapid oral absorption for related BTK inhibitors. The L1/L2 low-F contexts are structurally unrelated and do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20% in this pyrazolopyrimidine acrylamide. The fed-state condition is not directly tested for the query and does not override the absorption evidence."
}

